# Supplied documents that are served byte-for-byte.
#
# These files are returned to the browser unchanged by their route handlers, so
# their bytes are part of the deliverable. This repository is worked on from
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite their line endings to
# CRLF in the working copy — every line a byte longer than the file that was
# supplied and signed off. `-text` switches that conversion off in both
# directions, so what is checked out is what was committed, on any platform.
#
# Line endings do not change how a browser renders HTML. The point is that
# "byte-for-byte" stays literally true and verifiable with a checksum, rather
# than being true only on the machine that happens to have the right setting.
src/content/tools/*.html   -text
src/content/apple-ads-guide.html   -text
